 "text": "Hi, how's life been treating you? Use gentle pressure and rotate the brush rather than pulling it straight out. Also, wash it right after you use it, before the paint drys. That's fine as long as you use them within few weeks. A dry brush is much less effective. Try holding them at different angles while you paint, and use a little more pressure. It shouldn't take too long. If they're really bad, you can cut off the worn part and keep the sharp end. Many people do this and buy new handles whenever they want fresh brush.",
